WEBVTT


00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.194
<i>(woman sings in Bengali)</i>


00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.279
<i>(woman) I have a song in my head.</i>


00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.436
<i># Ranga mathay chironee</i>


00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.551
<i># Bor ashbay ekhonee</i>


00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.513
<i># Niye labay thokhonee</i>


00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:01.071
<i>I remember the songs we used to sing,
my sister and I.</i>


00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:30.595
<i>(gasps)</i>


00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.153
<i>(child laughs)</i>


00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:38.758
<i>I always said, "I will not marry
and be sent far away. "</i>


00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.555
<i>"I will go no further
than these paddy fields. "</i>


00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.596
<i>But our mother told us
we must not run from our fate.</i>


00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:56.158
<i>What cannot be changed must be borne.</i>


00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:01.079
<i>The test of life is to endure.</i>


00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.110
<i>(Bengali)</i>


00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.715
<i>But our mother could not endure.</i>


00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:10.276
<i>Amma.</i>


00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.912
<i>No one spoke of our mother's death,
and I remembered her saying:</i>


00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:32.672
<i>"If Allah wanted us to ask questions
he would have made us men. "</i>


00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.872
<i>Our fate was decided then.</i>


00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.477
<i>(Bengali)</i>


00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:53.037
<i>I was to be grateful when Father chose
me an educated man living abroad.</i>


00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:01.795
<i>My sister would stay.
I would go.</i>


00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:04.712
<i>You can spread your soul
over a paddy field.</i>


00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:07.673
<i>You can feel the earth
beneath your toes</i>


00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:10.268
<i>and know that this is the place,</i>


00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:13.995
<i>the place that it begins and ends.</i>


00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.917
<i>But what can you tell to a pile of bricks?</i>


00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:23.555
<i>I think of my sister.
I think of home.</i>


00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:29.273
<i>My husband promises me
we will be coming home soon.</i>


00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.512
Good.


00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:21.637
Good.


00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:25.671
I will test you both on your Tagore tonight.


00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:26.949
<i>(girl) OK. Abba.</i>


00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:29.753
Do you hear me. Shahana?


00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:34.158
- Abba, will you get the promotion today?
- Verv likely. Verv likely.


00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:36.271
<i>- (Nazneen) Get your lunchbox.
- OK.</i>


00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.709
My colleague Wilkie
thinks he will get the iob.


00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:41.752
Feet up on his desk in Mr Dalloway's office.


00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.917
Using the telephone at the lunchtime.


00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:50.514
I said to him,
"They need an educated man like me."


00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:54.192
They will not pass me over this time.


00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.788
Shahana. Sit up.


00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:00.879
If I just get the promotion confirmed


00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:04.231
then many things are possible.


00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:07.677
Don't cut the meat verv small.


00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:11.679
I need big pieces tonight
for dinner with Dr Azad.


00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.875
- Good luck with your promotion.
- It's from Auntie Hasina.


00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:21.557
So, who has your sister
fallen in love with today?


00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:25.590
<i>(Bengali)</i>


00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:30.271
<i>(father) Come on, Bibi, Shahana. Hurry
up. You can't be late for the school.</i>


00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:51.079
<i>(Hasina in Bengali)</i>


00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:53.794
<i>Do you tell your daughters
the story of the princess</i>


00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:57.310
<i>who lived seven seas and 13 rivers away?</i>


00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:01.035
<i>That is how I think of you in your tall tower.</i>


00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:03.276
<i>Now I cook for the lute men.</i>


00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:07.109
<i>I tell them of my sister living in London.</i>


00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:12.954
<i>There is one I like.
His skin is like lassi.</i>


00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:15.116
<i>I can see your worried face.</i>


00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.276
<i>But there is no need.</i>


00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:21.873
<i>When will you ever come home?</i>


00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:25.196
<i>(laughter)</i>


00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:32.279
Tariq! Stop messing around
with the sewing machine.


00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.118
<i>Acha go Amma!</i>


00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.037
- Oh, hello, Razia.
- Hello.


00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:38.913
<i>(woman) How do you like living
the other side of the block?</i>


00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:41.873
<i>(Razia) I'll tell you when I've moved in.
How's your hip?</i>


00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:44.878
<i>(woman) Oh. Verv painful.</i>


00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.309
Oh. Hello. Mrs Ahmed.


00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.159
You two are going to be neighbours.


00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:53.674
<i>- Salaam-alaikum.
- Salaam.</i>


00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:01.070
<i>(whispers) She keeps herself to herself.
She has two daughters.</i>


00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.872
But she lost her first.


00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:07.232
Such a boy.
The devil always takes beautiful babies.


00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:09.749
Have you heard about Zorina?


00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:13.793
<i>(Nazneen) Allah, place light in my heart,
light in my tongue.</i>


00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:18.277
<i>Light in my hearing,
light on my right hand. On my left.</i>


00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:23.428
<i>Light before me, light behind me,
light above me and light below me.</i>


00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:26.233
<i>Allah, who knows
the secrets of our hearts.</i>


00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:29.989
<i>Lead me out of the darkness
and give me light.</i>


00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.673
<i>(door closes)</i>


00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:55.756
Your coat?


00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.676
Is everything OK?


00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:15.398
I resigned this afternoon.


00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.273
They do not appreciate my talents.


00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:22.473
But I'm not worried.
I have some verv good leads I will chase...


00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:25.396
in the morning.


00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:33.116
You know. When I left the council office


00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:36.630
Mr Dalloway shook my hand.


00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:39.274
He was sorrv he was losing a good man.


00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:41.868
<i>(laughs)</i>


00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.231
We must be on our best behaviour tonight.


00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:49.473
"Ah. What thrill in autumn. O mother mine.


00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:54.196
In full-blossomed paddy fields I have
seen spread all over sweet smiles."


00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:57.198
"Ah, what beauty, what shades,
what affection and what..."


00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.436
Shahana.


00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:02.358
You will take over from your sister now.


00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.794
"What a guilt..."


00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:14.870
"What a quilt you have spread
at the feet of banyan trees


00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:16.877
and along the banks of rivers."


00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:21.278
"O mother mine, words from your lips
are like nectar to my ears."


00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:24.119
"Ah. What thrill is sadness."


00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:27.235
"O mother mine.


00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:30.079
Cast a gloom on your face.


00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:32.509
My eyes fill up with tears."


00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:34.198
<i>(applause)</i>


00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:37.153
A little more inflection next time.


00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:39.950
But better.


00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:53.035
<i>(laughter)</i>


00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:23.636
<i>- Salaam, Razia.
- Wa-alaikum-salaam.</i>


00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:25.478
- Got a lot for you this time.
- Good.


00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:29.195
I need to make enough
to keep the kids happy.


00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:40.758
<i>(Nazneen) Some of the women
are sewing at home. Even I...</i>


00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:42.950
Will you smarten me up a little?


00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:52.709
Which do you think
is the happiest nation on earth.


00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:56.799
Ranked number one
in the world's happiest survey?


00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:02.236
- Bangladesh.
- I'm worried about my sister.


00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:05.238
All along I've been telling her
we are coming home.


00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:07.749
She has... she has met someone.


00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:09.359
No. No. No. No.


00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:12.074
My cousin is not going to go
and rescue her again.


00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:14.475
If he could just visit her once...


00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:18.513
Maybe I could go. I could go
and walk around the streets and say:


00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:21.393
"Have you seen my wife's sister?"


00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.750
"She cooks for the jute men."


00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:29.310
I only have a job to find
and children to feed.


00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:33.437
But what of our plans to go home?


00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:35.630
I will work my contacts.


00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:39.316
But you were so sure of the promotion.


00:15:39.440 --> 00:15:41.635
They gave it to Wilkie.


00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:47.709
- Wilkie got the promotion?
- Wilkie got the promotion.


00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:51.196
People here are by and large ignorant


00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:55.154
and know nothing of the Bront雜


00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:57.236
and Thackeray.


00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:01.153
Can Wilkie guote from Chaucer?


00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.193
No. He cannot.


00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:11.071
Don't worry. I will have new employment
by the end of the week.


00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.714
I will clear my office today.


00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.359
<i>(sighs)</i>


00:16:58.480 --> 00:17:01.438
Oh! I've got them.


00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:04.917
Thank you.


00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:07.676
- I'm Razia.
- Hello.


00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:11.428
You want to have some tea?


00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:14.233
I haven't unpacked yet. But... come.


00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:16.316
Hm?


00:17:20.360 --> 00:17:23.397
I just got it. 12 speeds.


00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:27.074
�5.99 over 49 weeks.


00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:36.632
My daughter did it. I was fed up
with all that brushing and brushing.


00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:40.958
She wants to do hair and beauty at college,
but I'm hoping universitv if she works hard.


00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:43.116
- Bye, Amma.
- Bye.


00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:45.879
<i>(daughter) Love you.</i>


00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:49.709
Tariq. Always needing money
for his books.


00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:53.515
However much you give,
they always need more.


00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:58.796
What can you do?


00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:02.678
You'll need a machine.


00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:28.157
I'll send the boy over once you've practised.
You can earn a pound a piece.


00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:29.235
<i>(laughter)</i>


00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:32.158
<i>- (Nazneen) Bibi.
- I can see you. Amma.</i>


00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:35.238
<i>- I can see your feet.
- (Shahana) Let me measure your head.</i>


00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:37.430
<i>(Nazneen) Shahana!</i>


00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:39.437
Trv mine. Trv mine. Trv mine.


00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:46.558
- How big is my head?
- For a small brain. You have a big head.


00:18:55.880 --> 00:18:57.950
<i>(Bibi) Hello. Abba.</i>


00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:14.236
What is this?


00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:24.199
I will take the television. Then.


00:19:33.240 --> 00:19:35.435
It is a pound a piece.


00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:38.190
I will take food in my room.


00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:44.190
<i>(TV) Chiswick Auction House,
West London.</i>


00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:48.632
<i>Just down the road from where
the great painter Hogarth lived.</i>


00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:07.953
<i>(Nazneen) Sister, my husband says
a loss of pride is a terrible thing.</i>


00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:12.191
<i>But pride won't buy us tickets home.</i>


00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:18.434
<i>I have work now. Lust like you.</i>


00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:22.155
<i>I sew, and every hem
brings me closer to you.</i>


00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:27.557
<i>(Bengali)</i>


00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:02.076
<i>(knock at door)</i>


00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:09.390
<i>Huno Abba.</i>


00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:12.751
<i>Ami aimune aicha... Aicha.</i>


00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:17.751
<i>- Salaam-alaikum.
- Salaam.</i>


00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:21.196
Your husband in?


00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:27.555
It's OK. I visit a lot of the women.
If it's OK with him...


00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:49.359
This is a test batch.
Jeans. 42 pairs.


00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:54.075
<i>(phone rings)</i>


00:21:58.800 --> 00:22:02.873
<i>(Bengali)</i>


00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:15.310
Yeah, Abba.
See you later.


00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:22.238
My dad, always calling me
when I'm at work.


00:22:22.360 --> 00:22:24.954
Parents are always worrving.


00:22:27.720 --> 00:22:29.756
I'll pay you Thursday. OK?


00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:36.635
- Thank you.
- Don't thank me. It's a chore. Man.


00:22:42.200 --> 00:22:45.670
<i>- Salaam-alaikum.
- My mum had a sari like that.</i>


00:22:49.560 --> 00:22:51.516
<i>Wa-alaikum-salaam.</i>


00:23:05.760 --> 00:23:10.117
<i>- (Bibi) What is it, Abba?
- This is a birthday present for your mother.</i>


00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:14.313
- Her birthday's ages away.
- I'm also thinking about the home fund.


00:23:14.440 --> 00:23:16.032
<i>(Nazneen) Wait. Bibi!</i>


00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:20.392
There are some uneducated types
who believe if the wife is working.


00:23:20.520 --> 00:23:24.149
It is because the man
cannot put the food on the table.


00:23:24.280 --> 00:23:27.909
Lucky your mother
married an educated man.


00:23:28.040 --> 00:23:30.793
So you have found new employment?


00:23:30.920 --> 00:23:32.956
I've been told by a reliable source


00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:37.153
that they are in much need of lecturers
at Dhaka Universitv.


00:23:37.280 --> 00:23:41.478
To teach sociology, for example,
or philosophy.


00:23:42.440 --> 00:23:47.195
From today, we are joining
the world wide web.


00:23:47.320 --> 00:23:49.754
I will email them straightaway.


00:23:50.440 --> 00:23:52.351
But...


00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:54.835
where did the money come from?


00:23:58.600 --> 00:24:02.195
<i>(Bibi) Can I open this one for you. Abba?</i>


00:24:02.320 --> 00:24:05.232
One has to speculate to accumulate.


00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:07.669
What shall we start with?


00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:11.031
I can access the entire world.


00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:22.030
Too boring for the memsahib?


00:24:28.360 --> 00:24:29.918
What is the wrong with you?


00:24:30.040 --> 00:24:33.271
<i>You mean. "What is wrong with you?"</i>


00:24:36.560 --> 00:24:39.028
OK.


00:24:39.160 --> 00:24:41.913
From now on. No one speaks English.


00:24:44.160 --> 00:24:47.789
- You said that last time.
- Your behaviour is getting bad to worse!


00:24:47.920 --> 00:24:48.955
<i>(Bengali)</i>


00:24:49.080 --> 00:24:51.071
This is what they teach you
at the school?


00:24:51.200 --> 00:24:55.716
This is what they teach you?!
I will not allow this to happen!


00:24:55.840 --> 00:24:58.991
To learn manners
and to respect her father!


00:24:59.120 --> 00:25:02.112
<i>(Shahana) I didn't ask to be born here!</i>


00:25:04.760 --> 00:25:08.036
<i>(Bengali)</i>


00:25:15.040 --> 00:25:16.996
<i>(snoring)</i>


00:26:08.800 --> 00:26:11.553
Go home. You fucking Pakis!


00:26:16.280 --> 00:26:18.236
<i>(knock at door)</i>


00:26:19.880 --> 00:26:21.598
<i>Salaam-alaikum.</i>


00:26:21.720 --> 00:26:23.597
Sorrv about this.


00:26:24.640 --> 00:26:27.712
- What happened?
- I know who they are.


00:26:27.840 --> 00:26:31.116
The Lion Hearts. They've gone.


00:26:31.240 --> 00:26:33.800
I took it right from under their nose. Man.


00:26:35.280 --> 00:26:39.751
"Multicultural murder. Do you know
Britain is being slowly suffocated?"


00:26:39.880 --> 00:26:44.556
"Muslim extremists taking over our streets."


00:26:44.680 --> 00:26:46.910
- Who does all this?
- Idiots.


00:26:48.160 --> 00:26:50.230
You're thirstv.


00:27:12.040 --> 00:27:14.110
This is nice work.


00:27:17.680 --> 00:27:19.875
There's a pair missing.


00:27:21.400 --> 00:27:24.233
42. There should be 42.


00:27:26.280 --> 00:27:27.872
No.


00:27:28.000 --> 00:27:29.752
It's probably my mistake.


00:27:30.600 --> 00:27:32.556
<i>(phone rings)</i>


00:27:34.680 --> 00:27:36.955
- Father?
- My dad.


00:27:39.200 --> 00:27:42.112
25 years as a bus conductor,
now he doesn't leave the flat.


00:27:42.240 --> 00:27:45.869
Just ringing me all the time.
Every day the same.


00:27:47.680 --> 00:27:50.148
And your mother?


00:27:50.280 --> 00:27:52.236
Died five years ago.


00:27:55.440 --> 00:27:59.228
"Don't make trouble for yourself."
That's all my dad ever says to me.


00:27:59.360 --> 00:28:02.193
It's too many years
getting called all the names.


00:28:02.320 --> 00:28:05.437
Kids giving him cheek,
men giving him aggro.


00:28:06.080 --> 00:28:08.799
He never made trouble
for anyone his whole life.


00:28:08.920 --> 00:28:10.035
Tsk!


00:28:10.160 --> 00:28:13.994
He thinks he's Mahatma Gandhi.
He thinks he's Jesus Christ.


00:28:14.120 --> 00:28:17.874
Always saying to me,
"Turn the other cheek."


00:28:19.760 --> 00:28:21.716
That's what you get. Man.


00:28:22.760 --> 00:28:24.830
Yes. It's what you get.


00:28:28.240 --> 00:28:30.879
- A lot of books.
- My husband.


00:28:45.560 --> 00:28:49.348
I'm reading a very interesting book
at the moment.


00:28:49.480 --> 00:28:54.634
According to Hume, all objects of human
inguirv may be divided into two kinds.


00:28:54.760 --> 00:28:58.435
That is relation of ideas
and matters of fact.


00:28:59.240 --> 00:29:04.439
To explain the meaning of relation of idea,
Hume gives an example.


00:29:04.560 --> 00:29:09.190
That the three times of five
is egual to half of 30.


00:29:09.320 --> 00:29:11.276
Are you resting?


00:29:12.560 --> 00:29:15.233
This one is nice.


00:29:15.360 --> 00:29:21.230
I can say that it is nice or not nice, and
how can I be wrong. According to Hume?


00:29:21.360 --> 00:29:26.275
The search for knowledge -
is there anything more satisfying?


00:29:27.440 --> 00:29:33.151
The foundation of modern philosophy -
it is a verv interesting module.


00:29:34.480 --> 00:29:37.711
Hume also says that the sun...


00:29:40.320 --> 00:29:44.950
<i>(Hasina) Praise be to Allah.
So much to thank him for.</i>


00:29:45.080 --> 00:29:47.116
<i>I have news.</i>


00:29:47.240 --> 00:29:52.189
<i>I have accepted a proposal from Mr Lassi,
with his skin so white...</i>


00:29:53.720 --> 00:29:55.870
- Shahana.
- "Sister. We are married."


00:29:56.000 --> 00:30:00.152
"People stop and stare because
he is Mr Lassi and I am now his wife."


00:30:00.280 --> 00:30:02.475
Give it back. Shahana!


00:30:02.600 --> 00:30:04.192
Shahana. Give... Shahana!


00:30:04.320 --> 00:30:06.993
"I enjoy their stares,
walking arm in arm together."


00:30:07.120 --> 00:30:10.192
"I am in love, sister.
I am in love!"


00:30:12.520 --> 00:30:14.476
What is this?


00:30:15.800 --> 00:30:19.793
- I was just trying them on.
- Shahana. Off! Off. I said.


00:30:19.920 --> 00:30:23.071
- Shahana! Give it back.
- That's romantic. Man.


00:30:23.200 --> 00:30:26.317
What's Auntie like?
Is she like me?


00:30:26.440 --> 00:30:29.432
As pretty as you and as naughtv as you.


00:30:31.800 --> 00:30:35.156
At least her life is exciting.
At least it's not boring.


00:30:35.280 --> 00:30:39.956
- The test of life is to endure.
- I know. Amma. You tell me all the time.


00:30:40.080 --> 00:30:42.071
And so did my Amma.


00:30:42.200 --> 00:30:44.919
- Please! Ple...
- Shh! Bibi's sleeping.


00:30:45.040 --> 00:30:47.076
- Please. Please.
- No. No.


00:30:51.360 --> 00:30:53.316
Give it to me.


00:30:54.640 --> 00:30:56.676
"Walking arm in arm."


00:30:56.800 --> 00:30:58.711
"I am in love. Sister."


00:30:58.840 --> 00:31:01.149
"I am so in love."


00:31:01.280 --> 00:31:06.274
<i>(Hasina) I thought I knew love before,
but it was not like this.</i>


00:31:06.400 --> 00:31:11.030
<i>He's always watching me,
never letting me out of his sight.</i>


00:31:11.160 --> 00:31:13.355
<i>Like I might vanish.</i>


00:31:13.480 --> 00:31:16.950
<i>This time. I am sure it is right.</i>


00:31:17.080 --> 00:31:21.358
<i>(Bengali)</i>


00:31:46.040 --> 00:31:47.996
Thank you.


00:31:50.960 --> 00:31:53.235
Talk to me.


00:31:54.080 --> 00:31:56.548
This won't sew itself.


00:31:56.680 --> 00:31:58.636
You talk. I will listen.


00:32:07.040 --> 00:32:10.999
So many kids, man,
smoking shit. Doing nothing.


00:32:14.520 --> 00:32:16.431
Do you only go out with your husband?


00:32:16.560 --> 00:32:18.630
I go out when I need to shop.


00:32:20.680 --> 00:32:23.399
How long have you been living here?


00:32:24.320 --> 00:32:26.629
16 years.


00:32:26.760 --> 00:32:29.194
My mum came over when she was 17.


00:32:31.400 --> 00:32:33.356
- Me too.
- For real?


00:32:35.640 --> 00:32:37.596
You look younger.


00:32:43.120 --> 00:32:45.111
You know. When I was young.


00:32:45.240 --> 00:32:47.959
If you wanted to be cool,
you had to be something else.


00:32:48.080 --> 00:32:50.753
A bit white. A bit black. A bit something.


00:32:50.880 --> 00:32:52.871
Anything but Bangladeshi.


00:32:53.960 --> 00:32:56.110
<i>(Bengali)</i>


00:32:59.720 --> 00:33:00.709
What?


00:33:00.840 --> 00:33:03.354
You always stammer
when you talk Bengali.


00:33:04.880 --> 00:33:07.189
Only when I'm nervous.


00:33:14.880 --> 00:33:17.872
There's gonna be meetings every week.


00:33:18.720 --> 00:33:20.870
You should come.


00:33:22.120 --> 00:33:24.076
Bring your husband.


00:33:26.520 --> 00:33:28.476
<i>(knock at door)</i>


00:33:33.480 --> 00:33:37.029
<i>- Salaam-alaikum.
- Wa-alaikum-salaam.</i>


00:33:37.160 --> 00:33:39.515
<i>Salaam-alaikum.</i>


00:33:39.640 --> 00:33:41.596
Thursday.


00:33:47.520 --> 00:33:49.750
Your girls haven't been seen
at the madrasah.


00:33:49.880 --> 00:33:52.235
I will speak with my husband.


00:33:52.360 --> 00:33:54.316
Never mind.


00:33:55.800 --> 00:33:59.873
Place the money in the side pocket.
I won't count it.


00:34:08.880 --> 00:34:11.553
�50 as arranged.
Your husband owes me.


00:34:17.440 --> 00:34:20.398
I see how it is.
He hasn't talked to you.


00:34:20.920 --> 00:34:23.957
I will collect every week �50.


00:34:24.080 --> 00:34:27.152
It is simply an arrangement
between friends.


00:34:27.280 --> 00:34:29.669
Pay when you can.


00:34:29.800 --> 00:34:33.076
You will find a way.
Allah always gives a way.


00:34:35.440 --> 00:34:37.715
Ah. What a boy.


00:34:38.960 --> 00:34:40.916
Too beautiful.


00:34:45.920 --> 00:34:47.911
<i>(woman) Hello?</i>


00:34:49.600 --> 00:34:51.955
Anyone home?


00:34:55.880 --> 00:34:57.836
<i>(footsteps)</i>


00:35:01.160 --> 00:35:05.073
I hear her sons wanted
to buy her a hip replacement.


00:35:05.200 --> 00:35:06.838
"No. No. No. No. No."


00:35:06.960 --> 00:35:09.190
"Don't waste a good hip on me."


00:35:09.320 --> 00:35:12.198
"I don't want to be buried
with a new hip."


00:35:12.320 --> 00:35:14.709
"God does not love a wasteful woman."


00:35:14.840 --> 00:35:16.796
<i>(laughs)</i>


00:35:19.960 --> 00:35:23.635
My husband's borrowed money from her.


00:35:24.760 --> 00:35:27.149
How much she charge you?


00:35:27.280 --> 00:35:29.111
I don't know.


00:35:29.240 --> 00:35:31.470
How much does a computer cost?


00:35:31.600 --> 00:35:34.273
Certificates from everywhere.


00:35:34.400 --> 00:35:37.392
But your husband's a bloody fool.


00:35:37.520 --> 00:35:41.513
I know one family,
they've been paying six. Seven years.


00:35:41.640 --> 00:35:44.154
Whatever you pay,
she'll say you owe more.


00:35:44.280 --> 00:35:46.669
You'll never get rid of the debt.


00:35:46.800 --> 00:35:49.553
She's got a system
inherited from her husband.


00:35:49.680 --> 00:35:51.750
That's how usurers work.


00:35:51.880 --> 00:35:53.950
- She's a usurer?
- Mm.


00:35:55.160 --> 00:35:57.833
You take care.


00:35:57.960 --> 00:36:00.235
Zips and seams to finish.


00:36:04.680 --> 00:36:06.875
All right.


00:36:25.040 --> 00:36:27.031
<i>(Hasina in Bengali)</i>


00:37:26.200 --> 00:37:30.955
<i>(man) I suggest we call ourselves
United Muslim Action.</i>


00:37:31.080 --> 00:37:35.039
Let's get our own neighbourhood straight.
Show that Banglatown is defended.


00:37:35.160 --> 00:37:38.869
You ask what about Chechnya?
What about Palestine?


00:37:39.000 --> 00:37:41.468
Well. I say what about here?


00:37:42.720 --> 00:37:47.191
This community has been taking shit
from people like the Lion Hearts.


00:37:47.320 --> 00:37:50.517
What about your children?
Who's gonna fight for them?


00:37:50.640 --> 00:37:53.791
If we can't change things. Who can?


00:37:53.920 --> 00:37:57.151
I suggest we call ourselves Bengal Tigers.


00:37:57.280 --> 00:38:01.193
I say let's vote
and get Banglatown represented.


00:38:05.600 --> 00:38:07.955
Secretarv. Let's take a vote.


00:38:12.080 --> 00:38:15.675
- OK. Muslim Action?
- United Muslim Action.


00:38:15.800 --> 00:38:18.360
Bengal Tigers?


00:38:24.360 --> 00:38:27.193
Bengal Tigers is duly elected.


00:38:46.440 --> 00:38:48.396
I should go.


00:39:12.040 --> 00:39:13.996
Thursday?


00:39:14.120 --> 00:39:16.076
Mm.


00:40:26.320 --> 00:40:28.276
<i>(door opens)</i>


00:40:38.080 --> 00:40:41.789
<i>(Mr Ahmed) # Ekla cholo,
ekla cholo. Ekla cholore</i>


00:40:41.920 --> 00:40:45.549
<i># Jodi tor dak shuney
kew na ashey tobey</i>


00:40:45.680 --> 00:40:48.148
<i># Ekla cholore. Ekla cholo</i>


00:40:48.280 --> 00:40:51.556
<i># Ekla cholo, ekla cholo,
ekla cholore</i>


00:40:51.680 --> 00:40:52.795
<i>(Bengali)</i>


00:40:53.680 --> 00:40:56.877
As you are all aware,
your mother and I have decided


00:40:57.000 --> 00:40:59.355
that we as a family will return home.


00:40:59.880 --> 00:41:04.158
Your mother is doing everything
she can do to facilitate this trip.


00:41:04.280 --> 00:41:07.192
But today I have also become


00:41:07.320 --> 00:41:10.710
the employee of Kempton Cars.


00:41:10.840 --> 00:41:13.752
Driver 1619.


00:41:14.760 --> 00:41:16.876
So the home fund will prosper.


00:41:18.320 --> 00:41:20.595
Memsahib! Prepare!


00:41:22.120 --> 00:41:28.195
<i># Jodi tor dak shuney
kew na ashey tobey</i>


00:41:29.680 --> 00:41:31.875
<i>(Bibi) What's that. Abba?</i>


00:41:32.000 --> 00:41:34.753
Massage car seat cover.


00:41:34.880 --> 00:41:36.836
Verv good for back.


00:41:36.960 --> 00:41:40.953
For relief of tension
and unknotting of muscles.


00:41:41.080 --> 00:41:44.993
<i>- # La la la la la la la la
- (Bibi) Abba. Can I have a go?</i>


00:41:46.200 --> 00:41:49.317
All I have ever seen in this countrv


00:41:49.440 --> 00:41:52.159
is the Houses of Parliament.


00:41:52.280 --> 00:41:56.478
That was in 1979.


00:41:58.080 --> 00:42:00.389
So many years of struggling.


00:42:00.520 --> 00:42:03.512
I barely had time to lift my head


00:42:03.640 --> 00:42:05.596
and look around.


00:42:08.760 --> 00:42:10.955
<i>Oh, no, Alec, not here.
Someone will see.</i>


00:42:11.080 --> 00:42:13.150
<i>I love you so.</i>


00:42:17.560 --> 00:42:19.312
We must do some visiting.


00:42:20.480 --> 00:42:22.436
Sightseeing.


00:42:23.800 --> 00:42:25.756
<i>(mumbles)</i>


00:42:27.600 --> 00:42:30.353
<i>(Razia) Look how much these English
pay for their kameez.</i>


00:42:30.480 --> 00:42:33.153
It is giving you ideas.
This is too bright.


00:42:33.280 --> 00:42:34.998
And a rip-off.


00:42:35.120 --> 00:42:37.509
OK, I will leave you.
See you later.


00:42:37.640 --> 00:42:39.596
Bye.


00:42:49.040 --> 00:42:51.793
There's something I wanna show you.


00:43:12.000 --> 00:43:14.070
Where are you taking me?


00:43:20.240 --> 00:43:22.515
This is my uncle's factorv.


00:43:25.560 --> 00:43:27.630
Just closing up right now.


00:44:30.960 --> 00:44:32.712
<i>(door opens)</i>


00:44:55.200 --> 00:45:00.672
<i>(Nazneen) Sister, there is
something I must tell you.</i>


00:45:00.800 --> 00:45:05.351
<i>If you were here I would spend
so much time talking to you.</i>


00:45:05.480 --> 00:45:07.675
<i>Something is happening.</i>


00:45:07.800 --> 00:45:11.110
<i>I know it is foolish but I cannot help it.</i>


00:45:11.240 --> 00:45:14.676
<i>I tell myself. "Be careful. Be careful."</i>


00:47:55.520 --> 00:47:58.557
Children. Are you enioying yourself?


00:48:00.520 --> 00:48:05.640
You see? When you have all the time
in the world to see something.


00:48:05.760 --> 00:48:07.512
You don't bother to see it.


00:48:08.120 --> 00:48:12.159
Now that we are going home,
I have become a tourist.


00:48:12.280 --> 00:48:14.350
It is so ironic.


00:48:15.680 --> 00:48:18.956
"Buckingham Palace has been
the official residency


00:48:19.080 --> 00:48:21.230
of British sovereigns since 1837."


00:48:21.360 --> 00:48:25.512
- Do you have the cream? I'm going black.
- Shh. Your father is speaking.


00:48:25.640 --> 00:48:28.359
- If he ever stops, let me know.
- Shahana!


00:48:28.480 --> 00:48:32.314
Look, Shahana.
Look at this beautiful building.


00:48:32.440 --> 00:48:35.671
If you have historv. You have pride.


00:48:35.800 --> 00:48:39.759
People here know nothing
of our national heroes like... er...


00:48:39.880 --> 00:48:44.192
Like Colonel Osmani and also
Shah Jalal. Both from Sylhet.


00:48:44.760 --> 00:48:47.035
I know. I know who they are.


00:48:49.600 --> 00:48:50.999
<i>- Excuse me.
- (man) Yes.</i>


00:48:51.120 --> 00:48:52.997
- Can you take a picture for me?
- Sure.


00:48:53.120 --> 00:48:54.951
Turn. Turn. Turn.


00:48:55.080 --> 00:48:56.911
- Where are you from?
- Bangladesh.


00:48:57.040 --> 00:49:00.237
- What's he got to fiddle around for?
- I will buy you the earrings.


00:49:00.360 --> 00:49:02.351
The really long ones?


00:49:02.480 --> 00:49:04.869
Down to your knees.


00:49:05.000 --> 00:49:07.878
Now. Smile. Smile.


00:49:08.000 --> 00:49:09.956
OK. Ready.


00:49:14.560 --> 00:49:16.835
<i>- (grunts)
- (laughter)</i>


00:49:26.680 --> 00:49:29.240
<i>(Bibi) Amma. Stop.</i>


00:49:29.680 --> 00:49:34.356
<i>(Mr Ahmed) Are you feeling well?
Too much excitement. Perhaps.</i>


00:49:34.480 --> 00:49:38.439
See how happy your mother is
now we are going home.


00:49:56.120 --> 00:50:00.113
<i>(Nazneen) Sister, there is
something I have to tell you.</i>


00:50:01.320 --> 00:50:03.709
<i>I am...</i>


00:50:03.840 --> 00:50:05.796
<i>I am in...</i>


00:50:11.280 --> 00:50:13.236
<i>(crumples paper)</i>


00:50:20.160 --> 00:50:22.799
<i>Hasina. My husband thanks you.</i>


00:50:22.920 --> 00:50:25.673
<i>The pudina for his ulcer is working well.</i>


00:50:25.800 --> 00:50:29.793
<i>I am praying for you
and your new husband every day.</i>


00:50:33.320 --> 00:50:35.151
<i>(Nazneen) My sister.</i>


00:50:35.280 --> 00:50:38.829
She ran off with one of the men
who worked for my father.


00:50:40.120 --> 00:50:42.190
He never forgave her.


00:50:43.720 --> 00:50:46.075
They stole his bicycle.


00:50:55.120 --> 00:50:57.395
My boy.


00:51:00.560 --> 00:51:02.516
He was my first.


00:51:07.440 --> 00:51:10.193
I found him in his cot.


00:51:10.320 --> 00:51:12.276
He stopped breathing.


00:51:16.640 --> 00:51:19.108
We don't talk about it any more.


00:51:23.560 --> 00:51:25.835
He is beautiful.


00:51:30.440 --> 00:51:32.396
Yes.


00:51:35.520 --> 00:51:38.592
The devil only takes beautiful babies.


00:51:49.560 --> 00:51:51.516
What?


00:51:53.640 --> 00:51:56.029
Why do you like me?


00:52:00.160 --> 00:52:02.116
Who says I like you?


00:52:07.160 --> 00:52:09.151
There's two tvpes. Right?


00:52:09.880 --> 00:52:13.759
Your westernised girl,
into going out. Having a laugh.


00:52:13.880 --> 00:52:18.431
Short skirts as soon
as she's out of her father's sight.


00:52:18.560 --> 00:52:22.075
Then your religious girl.
You think they'd be good wife material


00:52:22.200 --> 00:52:25.795
but they ain't,
cos all they wanna do is argue.


00:52:26.720 --> 00:52:29.029
So what about me?


00:52:29.160 --> 00:52:30.991
You...


00:52:32.040 --> 00:52:33.996
you're the real thing.


00:52:35.480 --> 00:52:37.436
A girl from the village.


00:52:40.760 --> 00:52:43.399
Don't you ever want to go home?


00:52:47.600 --> 00:52:49.556
This is my home.


00:53:39.320 --> 00:53:41.276
<i>(woman) What's going on?</i>


00:53:42.040 --> 00:53:44.429
<i>(shouting)</i>


00:54:00.160 --> 00:54:02.390
<i>(Mr Ahmed) The world has gone mad.</i>


00:54:06.520 --> 00:54:07.475
<i>(speaks Bengali)</i>


00:54:07.600 --> 00:54:10.751
<i>(Bush) The search is under way
for those behind these evil acts.</i>


00:54:10.880 --> 00:54:15.271
<i>(Mr Ahmed) It will be just like when
I first arrived. There will be a backlash.</i>


00:54:15.960 --> 00:54:19.270
There has been enough planning.
Start packing.


00:54:19.400 --> 00:54:21.868
- We will be in Dhaka within the month.
- What?


00:54:22.000 --> 00:54:25.754
No more pop CDs.
All money goes to the home fund.


00:54:26.200 --> 00:54:28.031
- Ow!
- And cover your legs.


00:54:28.160 --> 00:54:31.072
Take more sewing.
We need more money.


00:54:31.200 --> 00:54:34.078
- I will speak to him.
- No!


00:54:37.240 --> 00:54:39.435
Who?


00:54:39.560 --> 00:54:41.949
Who you do not wish me to speak to?


00:54:43.840 --> 00:54:46.308
No-no... no one.


00:54:48.200 --> 00:54:50.031
I'll do it.


00:54:51.560 --> 00:54:55.155
- Do what?
- Speak... speak to him.


00:54:57.040 --> 00:54:58.598
Verv well.


00:54:58.720 --> 00:55:00.995
You tell him...


00:55:01.840 --> 00:55:04.798
you want paying extra 50�%


00:55:04.920 --> 00:55:07.150
if we are ever to get home.


00:55:09.320 --> 00:55:11.993
<i>(Blair)... carried out these attacks.</i>


00:55:12.120 --> 00:55:15.908
<i>There are no adequate
words of condemnation.</i>


00:55:16.040 --> 00:55:21.558
<i>Their barbarism will stand
as their shame for all eternity.</i>


00:55:24.840 --> 00:55:28.150
Community meeting.
Come along. Brother.


00:55:36.880 --> 00:55:38.950
<i>(Mr Ahmed) Shahana. Bibi.</i>


00:55:40.600 --> 00:55:43.160
Come on. Girls.


00:55:43.280 --> 00:55:46.955
<i>(man) Go! Go! You fucking terrorists!
Get out!</i>


00:55:47.080 --> 00:55:51.710
Go back to your own country,
you bin Ladens! Go on. Fuck off!


00:55:54.520 --> 00:55:58.877
<i>(TV) This has been a year of racial tension
in Britain. With race riots in the north.</i>


00:55:59.000 --> 00:56:01.878
<i>The fear is now
that this tension will increase.</i>


00:56:02.000 --> 00:56:07.028
<i>Many claim that in the last seven days,
"Muslim" has become a dirty word.</i>


00:56:07.160 --> 00:56:09.628
<i>(newsreader #2)
Broken windows at a mosque -</i>


00:56:09.760 --> 00:56:13.036
<i>a consequence of
these misconceptions.</i>


00:56:13.160 --> 00:56:16.709
<i>(woman) People say to us, "You
shouldn't be here. Why are you here?"</i>


00:56:16.840 --> 00:56:18.990
<i>"Go away."</i>


00:56:20.360 --> 00:56:25.195
It's getting crazy out there.
My dad's really scared now.


00:56:25.320 --> 00:56:29.598
Some white boy goes and pulls my
cousin's hiiab down in the street today.


00:56:29.720 --> 00:56:34.077
He was only about ten. I'm telling you, man,
things are changing.


00:56:34.200 --> 00:56:37.351
The way people look at you now
on the streets - so much mistrust.


00:56:37.480 --> 00:56:41.598
I wanna say, "If I was a bomber, do you
think I'd be carrving 50 pairs of ieans?"


00:56:41.720 --> 00:56:44.188
- Stop.
- What?


00:56:44.320 --> 00:56:46.197
<i>(door closes)</i>


00:56:55.080 --> 00:56:57.036
<i>Salaam-alaikum.</i>


00:57:06.920 --> 00:57:08.558
<i>Wa-alaikum-salaam.</i>


00:57:26.000 --> 00:57:29.197
- Is it interesting?
- I was just browsing.


00:57:29.320 --> 00:57:31.276
You don't mind?


00:57:33.400 --> 00:57:35.914
Why should I mind?


00:57:36.040 --> 00:57:38.429
When I was a young man like you.


00:57:38.560 --> 00:57:40.915
Do you know what I wanted to be?


00:57:41.760 --> 00:57:45.389
A British civil servant, right-hand
bloody man of the prime minister.


00:57:45.520 --> 00:57:48.193
And I saw no reason why not.


00:57:48.320 --> 00:57:51.551
Anything is possible when you are young.


00:57:57.280 --> 00:57:59.111
Then you get older.


00:57:59.240 --> 00:58:02.277
And the thing about getting older is...


00:58:03.600 --> 00:58:09.789
that you don't need everything
to be possible any more.


00:58:09.920 --> 00:58:12.957
You just need some things to be certain.


00:58:43.640 --> 00:58:46.234
<i>- (Shahana) Abba.
- Mm.</i>


00:58:46.360 --> 00:58:50.956
If you left me and Bibi behind,
you wouldn't have to save as much.


00:58:51.080 --> 00:58:53.435
And we could be adopted.


00:58:58.280 --> 00:59:01.158
Do you want me to beat you?


00:59:01.280 --> 00:59:02.918
Yes.


00:59:03.040 --> 00:59:06.350
Well. I won't beat you


00:59:06.480 --> 00:59:09.119
and I won't leave you behind.


00:59:09.920 --> 00:59:13.390
One day, Abba, I'll run
and you won't ever catch me.


00:59:13.840 --> 00:59:15.319
Shahana!


00:59:15.440 --> 00:59:17.396
<i>(door slams)</i>


00:59:20.880 --> 00:59:22.552
<i>(Bengali)</i>


00:59:22.680 --> 00:59:25.558
Why did Allah curse me with daughters?!


00:59:25.680 --> 00:59:27.079
Shahana!


00:59:29.440 --> 00:59:31.829
Shahana!


00:59:31.960 --> 00:59:36.829
Do you think your cheek
will serve you well in the world?


00:59:36.960 --> 00:59:41.078
Can you imagine the things
I have had to fight?


00:59:43.280 --> 00:59:48.718
Do you know what you're going to have
to face out there every day?


00:59:48.840 --> 00:59:50.796
Every day.


00:59:53.120 --> 00:59:54.712
Shahana.


00:59:56.400 --> 01:00:01.838
Do you think I'm like this
for the good of my health?


01:00:03.080 --> 01:00:05.036
No. Abba.


01:00:08.840 --> 01:00:10.796
Good.


01:00:11.840 --> 01:00:14.479
I am glad


01:00:14.600 --> 01:00:18.229
we have talked
father and daughter like this.


01:00:39.080 --> 01:00:40.911
<i>(Nazneen) Sister...</i>


01:00:41.960 --> 01:00:44.190
<i>I have an unquiet mind.</i>


01:00:47.120 --> 01:00:50.556
<i>And it is so long
since I have heard from you.</i>


01:01:06.800 --> 01:01:08.597
It was still on the mat.


01:01:10.840 --> 01:01:12.990
You must have been busy.


01:01:15.000 --> 01:01:18.879
You think she's enioying married life?


01:01:20.280 --> 01:01:23.590
My cousin says she has left her husband.


01:01:24.880 --> 01:01:27.997
He has seen her working the hotels.


01:01:28.120 --> 01:01:32.477
It is where all the... floating girls go.


01:01:38.280 --> 01:01:42.478
You think she lived off cooking
all these years?


01:01:42.600 --> 01:01:46.957
All these years, all these letters,
hearing what your sister had to say.


01:01:47.080 --> 01:01:48.399
Give me my letter!


01:01:48.520 --> 01:01:52.149
Maybe I should have been asking
what you are writing to her.


01:01:52.280 --> 01:01:57.400
Give it to me. Give it to me! I said give!
Give me my letter! Give! Give!


01:01:57.520 --> 01:02:00.353
You are no different to your sister!


01:02:09.680 --> 01:02:12.990
<i>(Hasina) Sister. Mr Lassi has gone.</i>


01:02:13.120 --> 01:02:15.998
<i>Hussain from the factory
has been very kind to me.</i>


01:02:16.120 --> 01:02:18.270
<i>He brings me a little food.</i>


01:02:18.400 --> 01:02:21.631
<i>Haven't I always known
how to take care of myself?</i>


01:02:21.760 --> 01:02:24.194
<i>We all survive in different ways.</i>


01:02:31.280 --> 01:02:34.636
<i>Last night was so funny.
I sang for Rehan.</i>


01:02:34.760 --> 01:02:37.957
<i>He makes me sit on the bed
like when he first saw me.</i>


01:02:38.080 --> 01:02:42.437
<i>Mr Chowdhury is like a father to me.
He treats me very well.</i>


01:02:42.560 --> 01:02:45.632
<i>They tease me,
but I know they're only loking.</i>


01:02:45.760 --> 01:02:49.116
<i>- Ahmed likes to bring me to his house.
- (Mr Ahmed) Are you all right?</i>


01:02:49.240 --> 01:02:53.438
<i>I do not tell him I'm a married woman.
I have never been good at staying still.</i>


01:02:53.560 --> 01:02:56.358
<i>Abba went with other women.</i>


01:02:56.960 --> 01:03:01.397
<i>Mr Chowdhury says
these boys are like moths to a flame.</i>


01:03:08.920 --> 01:03:11.309
<i>I won't be like Amma.</i>


01:03:11.440 --> 01:03:13.556
<i>She took the forbidden path.</i>


01:03:13.680 --> 01:03:16.433
<i>She did not endure. So why should we?</i>


01:03:28.280 --> 01:03:30.236
<i>(woman in Bengali)</i>


01:03:33.440 --> 01:03:36.477
Amma. Amma. She's sleeping.


01:03:47.080 --> 01:03:49.514
She wakes.


01:03:55.480 --> 01:03:57.948
Will you have some food now?


01:03:58.920 --> 01:04:01.354
Just a little rice.


01:04:01.480 --> 01:04:03.277
Rice it is.


01:04:04.320 --> 01:04:07.995
Dr Azad said the illness
will leave you hungrv.


01:04:14.720 --> 01:04:19.111
<i>(TV)... of the US-led bombardment.
The rally was told another malor...</i>


01:04:27.320 --> 01:04:29.595
I started to pack.


01:04:32.240 --> 01:04:34.310
Oh. Wait.


01:04:53.160 --> 01:04:54.559
How?


01:04:54.680 --> 01:04:58.036
Where there is a will. There is always a way.


01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:03.879
What should I take -
Thackeray or the Proust?


01:05:04.000 --> 01:05:06.036
I will take both.


01:05:08.160 --> 01:05:10.196
You rest now.


01:05:11.320 --> 01:05:15.279
Now, where are my certificates?
Do you know what Gandhi said


01:05:15.400 --> 01:05:18.233
when asked what he thought
about Western civilisation?


01:05:18.360 --> 01:05:22.717
<i>He said he thought
it would be a good idea. (laughs)</i>


01:05:23.920 --> 01:05:25.990
<i>(Razia) When do you go?</i>


01:05:28.760 --> 01:05:31.558
The tickets are booked in three weeks.


01:05:32.200 --> 01:05:33.952
So. Have you seen him?


01:05:35.040 --> 01:05:37.315
- Karim?
- No.


01:05:38.720 --> 01:05:40.756
Did he visit while I was ill?


01:05:40.880 --> 01:05:43.872
Haven't seen him for days.
Someone said he's away.


01:05:46.000 --> 01:05:48.560
Don't make trouble for yourself.


01:05:50.560 --> 01:05:52.516
I already have.


01:05:56.880 --> 01:05:59.872
- It looks like you are doing well.
- Mm.


01:06:02.280 --> 01:06:04.840
I'll need people to sew.


01:06:06.400 --> 01:06:08.356
<i>(doorbell)</i>


01:06:17.040 --> 01:06:18.996
<i>Salaam-alaikum.</i>


01:07:05.400 --> 01:07:07.755
You are angrv with me.


01:07:07.880 --> 01:07:10.314
No.


01:07:10.440 --> 01:07:12.396
I've been away.


01:07:13.600 --> 01:07:16.558
Visiting family in Bradford.


01:07:16.680 --> 01:07:21.390
If I'd known you was ill...
I can see you're angrv with me.


01:07:21.520 --> 01:07:26.719
Why do you not believe me when
I tell you that I'm not angrv with you?


01:07:32.200 --> 01:07:35.192
I turned down a girl last week for you.


01:07:38.200 --> 01:07:40.236
My dad keeps asking me why.


01:07:43.160 --> 01:07:44.832
What can I do?


01:07:44.960 --> 01:07:48.316
You could stay. He could go.
Let him divorce you.


01:07:48.760 --> 01:07:50.478
We'll get married.


01:07:50.600 --> 01:07:52.556
I'll sort it.


01:07:56.520 --> 01:07:59.398
<i>- And then what?
- (door opens)</i>


01:07:59.520 --> 01:08:02.034
<i>(Shahana) Amma.</i>


01:08:14.640 --> 01:08:16.596
<i>(door slams)</i>


01:08:20.600 --> 01:08:22.750
Good night.


01:08:22.880 --> 01:08:25.440
Are you in love with him?


01:08:26.360 --> 01:08:29.716
I mean, have you ever been
in love with him?


01:08:29.840 --> 01:08:31.910
Maybe before he got fat?


01:08:33.640 --> 01:08:35.073
<i>(Bengali)</i>


01:08:35.200 --> 01:08:39.432
We don't have to go, Amma.
You don't have to go.


01:08:39.560 --> 01:08:41.437
We shall wait and see.


01:08:41.560 --> 01:08:44.074
That's no answer.


01:08:44.200 --> 01:08:46.634
It is my answer. Good night.


01:08:53.480 --> 01:08:56.870
<i>(Nazneen) Sister,
may Allah take care of you.</i>


01:08:57.000 --> 01:09:02.074
<i>I'm sending you a little more money
to help keep you safe.</i>


01:09:02.200 --> 01:09:04.555
<i>How long have we been talking?</i>


01:09:05.680 --> 01:09:09.150
<i>How long have I not been hearing
what you say?</i>


01:09:11.440 --> 01:09:13.476
<i>I too have secrets.</i>


01:09:14.440 --> 01:09:16.510
<i>Now is the time for truth.</i>


01:09:18.120 --> 01:09:20.953
<i>I feel as if I'm waking from a dream.</i>


01:09:22.680 --> 01:09:24.671
<i>The world is changing.</i>


01:09:24.800 --> 01:09:26.552
<i>And me with it.</i>


01:09:28.280 --> 01:09:30.316
<i>We are coming home.</i>


01:09:30.440 --> 01:09:32.510
<i>How can we stay?</i>


01:09:34.400 --> 01:09:36.675
<i>(Bibi) Amma.</i>


01:09:45.960 --> 01:09:49.430
<i>- (Shahana) Bibi, look at that!
- (cheering)</i>


01:09:51.120 --> 01:09:53.076
<i>(woman) Mrs Ahmed!</i>


01:09:55.320 --> 01:09:59.632
I know you have been ill.
Just give me what you owe.


01:09:59.760 --> 01:10:01.591
How would it look if I let you off?


01:10:01.720 --> 01:10:04.632
Let one slip. They all slip through.


01:10:05.920 --> 01:10:10.072
Your husband is trying to run away,
but I won't let him.


01:10:10.200 --> 01:10:15.274
He comes asking for more and I tell him,
"Pay what you owe."


01:10:15.400 --> 01:10:17.994
<i>- (boy) Shahana.
- What?</i>


01:10:19.560 --> 01:10:21.437
Who are they?


01:10:21.560 --> 01:10:23.915
Her friends from school.


01:10:34.600 --> 01:10:36.556
Ugh.


01:10:39.040 --> 01:10:40.075
Ugh!


01:10:40.200 --> 01:10:42.350
Bibi!


01:10:42.480 --> 01:10:45.950
In Bangladesh you have to brush
your teeth with a twig.


01:10:46.080 --> 01:10:48.150
And go toilet in a bucket.


01:10:49.680 --> 01:10:52.592
Auntie Hasina goes to the toilet
in a bucket next to a goat.


01:10:52.720 --> 01:10:54.711
- Shahana!
- It's true.


01:10:54.840 --> 01:10:56.717
Less talking. More brushing.


01:10:56.840 --> 01:10:58.796
It's true.


01:11:02.040 --> 01:11:04.679
Well. Do you even want to go?


01:11:08.640 --> 01:11:10.596
You don't.


01:11:12.000 --> 01:11:14.639
<i>(door closes)</i>


01:11:17.640 --> 01:11:20.791
What Mrs Islam says...


01:11:21.600 --> 01:11:23.716
Is this true?


01:11:23.840 --> 01:11:25.637
This is a good guestion.


01:11:26.400 --> 01:11:28.595
When you feel something so strongly.


01:11:28.720 --> 01:11:32.838
You have to ask yourself. "Is this true?"


01:11:37.800 --> 01:11:39.711
I still have my coat on.


01:11:40.800 --> 01:11:43.792
Isn't it fair to say that you hate it
when I come inside


01:11:43.920 --> 01:11:46.593
and forget to take it off?


01:12:00.080 --> 01:12:02.150
I'm not totally blind.


01:12:07.040 --> 01:12:09.315
Don't worrv.


01:12:09.440 --> 01:12:13.353
A little business venture I have in mind.


01:12:13.800 --> 01:12:17.190
I'm gathering together samples.


01:12:19.880 --> 01:12:22.030
Soap is the future.


01:12:25.080 --> 01:12:28.117
I think we should go to this meeting.


01:12:28.240 --> 01:12:31.357
In fact. I have prepared a short speech.


01:12:33.920 --> 01:12:35.876
Will you come?


01:12:55.680 --> 01:12:59.514
<i>(man) Our fathers are being spat at,
our young brothers stopped and searched</i>


01:12:59.640 --> 01:13:02.108
again and again by
our so-called police force.


01:13:02.240 --> 01:13:05.038
Our sisters. They've been abused


01:13:05.160 --> 01:13:08.596
when they walk their little children
in the streets.


01:13:08.720 --> 01:13:11.598
Banglatown needs defending.


01:13:12.520 --> 01:13:18.231
Karim has a list of estates. We need
volunteers to wipe out this kind of filth.


01:13:19.320 --> 01:13:21.515
- Brother.
- Thanks. Bruv.


01:13:22.560 --> 01:13:27.509
Out there are people
twisted with hatred for us and Islam.


01:13:28.640 --> 01:13:30.915
We're gonna show them
how wrong they are.


01:13:31.040 --> 01:13:33.554
<i>(crowd) Yeah!</i>


01:13:33.680 --> 01:13:36.433
<i>(Karim) We've become victims,
but not for long!</i>


01:13:36.560 --> 01:13:37.993
<i>(crowd) Yeah!</i>


01:13:38.120 --> 01:13:42.033
We stand arm in arm with
our Muslim brothers ready to defend.


01:13:42.160 --> 01:13:43.513
Yeah!


01:13:43.640 --> 01:13:46.712
What is it you plan to defend?


01:13:47.840 --> 01:13:50.593
What is it you are planning to defend?


01:13:50.720 --> 01:13:53.154
<i>- (man) Islam, brother!
- (crowd shouts)</i>


01:13:53.280 --> 01:13:57.796
No, no, no, no, no, no. Let the brother
speak. Let the brother speak.


01:13:58.200 --> 01:14:01.715
<i>- You think Islam unites us all?
- (man) Yes.</i>


01:14:01.840 --> 01:14:04.877
You think Islam
is the place you come from?


01:14:05.000 --> 01:14:08.754
Islam is not a country.
You think you are my brother


01:14:08.880 --> 01:14:13.795
more than the next man on the street
because we are both Muslims?


01:14:15.960 --> 01:14:19.032
All this fighting talk that we are all brothers.


01:14:19.160 --> 01:14:24.632
Three million! Three million died
in East Pakistan in this lifetime.


01:14:24.760 --> 01:14:26.910
Not in my lifetime. Uncle.


01:14:27.040 --> 01:14:29.634
In your parents' lifetime.


01:14:29.760 --> 01:14:31.876
What was that?


01:14:32.000 --> 01:14:34.275
Brotherly love?


01:14:34.400 --> 01:14:36.914
It was Muslim killing a Muslim.


01:14:41.600 --> 01:14:43.477
Have you forgotten?


01:14:43.600 --> 01:14:45.556
Are you so lost?


01:14:49.280 --> 01:14:52.317
My Islam is in here.


01:14:53.720 --> 01:14:56.473
And that is the only thing worth defending.


01:14:56.600 --> 01:14:58.955
<i>- (man #1) Right.
- (man #2) Hear. Hear.</i>


01:14:59.080 --> 01:15:01.355
<i>(man #3) We plan to defend
against hatred.</i>


01:15:01.480 --> 01:15:03.596
We all stand together. Brothers.


01:15:04.640 --> 01:15:07.108
<i>(chairman) All right. All right. Moving on.</i>


01:15:07.240 --> 01:15:11.313
Our brother Karim has got the list
of all the local estates.


01:15:11.440 --> 01:15:14.557
<i>(fading) Everyone in here
has been allocated an area...</i>


01:15:47.080 --> 01:15:49.150
It is the time to go home.


01:16:11.000 --> 01:16:13.116
<i>- Salaam-alaikum.
- Wa-alaikum-salaam.</i>


01:16:13.240 --> 01:16:15.674
I've only got ten minutes.


01:16:16.320 --> 01:16:19.995
I've talked to some of the other brothers.
It's not looking good.


01:16:20.120 --> 01:16:22.156
I cannot marrv you.


01:16:24.080 --> 01:16:28.517
- Well, yeah, not straightaway, but...
- No. Um...


01:16:28.640 --> 01:16:30.710
<i>I do not want to marrv you.</i>


01:16:32.920 --> 01:16:35.195
Come on. Come.


01:16:41.360 --> 01:16:43.635
Look at me.


01:16:43.760 --> 01:16:46.274
Say it again.


01:16:46.400 --> 01:16:48.470
Look at me and say it.


01:16:50.200 --> 01:16:52.156
I do not want to marrv you. Karim.


01:16:52.280 --> 01:16:54.316
Right.


01:16:54.440 --> 01:16:56.670
Right. Right.


01:16:58.600 --> 01:17:00.955
You don't wanna marrv me?


01:17:01.080 --> 01:17:03.878
<i>(Bengali)</i>


01:17:10.520 --> 01:17:13.398
- Is it the sin of it? Is that it?
- No. No.


01:17:15.400 --> 01:17:18.039
Karim. That we have already done.


01:17:20.160 --> 01:17:21.718
I...


01:17:21.840 --> 01:17:24.559
I am not the real thing.


01:17:24.680 --> 01:17:27.148
I'm no longer a girl from the village.


01:17:27.280 --> 01:17:29.157
- Yes, you are.
- No.


01:17:29.840 --> 01:17:31.876
You just wanted me to be.


01:17:32.560 --> 01:17:34.437
We just made each other up.


01:17:34.560 --> 01:17:37.154
Well. What did you want?


01:17:39.800 --> 01:17:43.475
I just wanted to feel


01:17:43.600 --> 01:17:45.636
like I was at home.


01:17:48.600 --> 01:17:50.955
Karim.


01:17:51.960 --> 01:17:53.916
<i>(sniffs)</i>


01:17:56.120 --> 01:17:57.997
You better pray like hell.


01:17:58.120 --> 01:18:01.635
That's what I'm gonna do.
Allah forgives.


01:18:03.720 --> 01:18:05.756
<i>Salaam-alaikum.</i>


01:18:07.240 --> 01:18:09.196
<i>Wa-alaikum-salaam.</i>


01:18:41.560 --> 01:18:43.516
Hello?


01:18:44.040 --> 01:18:45.996
Hello?


01:18:55.680 --> 01:18:58.274
Mrs Ahmed?


01:18:58.400 --> 01:19:00.356
Hello?


01:19:02.200 --> 01:19:04.156
Hello?


01:19:16.200 --> 01:19:18.270
Just give me what you owe.


01:19:20.360 --> 01:19:22.396
I need my money.


01:19:25.360 --> 01:19:27.920
From the goodness of my heart. I give.


01:19:28.040 --> 01:19:31.157
And when those who receive
don't want to pay back what they owe.


01:19:31.280 --> 01:19:34.670
They run off to foreign countries
and say. "Why should we pay her?"


01:19:34.800 --> 01:19:37.792
- "She's just an old, sick woman."
- How much do you want?


01:19:37.920 --> 01:19:40.639
- �200 to settle the debt.
- No.


01:19:41.160 --> 01:19:44.436
We paid it all and some more as well.


01:19:44.560 --> 01:19:48.235
The money's for the madrasah.
But what is that to you?


01:19:48.360 --> 01:19:51.352
- �200 and settle it.
- But we paid what we owed!


01:19:51.480 --> 01:19:55.473
We paid at least �300 on top of that!
I'm not going to pay any more interest!


01:19:55.600 --> 01:19:58.114
<i>(coughs)</i>


01:19:58.240 --> 01:20:01.676
Do you think before God
I will charge interest?


01:20:01.800 --> 01:20:03.597
- Am I a money lender?
- No?


01:20:12.240 --> 01:20:17.951
Just swear on Koran that you're not
and I'll pay you the 200. Just swear on it!


01:20:19.040 --> 01:20:24.160
There are certain things a wife
does not want her husband to know.


01:20:26.440 --> 01:20:29.273
My husband knows everything.


01:20:29.400 --> 01:20:32.278
Just swear on the Koran.
That is all you have to do.


01:20:32.400 --> 01:20:34.868
Swear on it.


01:20:37.240 --> 01:20:39.629
Allah sees all your wrongs.


01:20:39.760 --> 01:20:42.752
Anyway. You have paid too much.


01:20:42.880 --> 01:20:45.348
- And he sees yours too.
- Huh!


01:20:58.720 --> 01:21:01.439
- We will store these boxes.
- OK. Mr Ahmed.


01:21:01.560 --> 01:21:04.279
The rest is for the auction. Thank you.


01:21:04.400 --> 01:21:06.356
<i>(hums cheerfully)</i>


01:21:14.520 --> 01:21:17.910
A colleague from Kempton Cars
will collect us.


01:21:18.040 --> 01:21:22.511
He is more or less an ignorant type
but a good-hearted man -


01:21:22.640 --> 01:21:25.074
as they say. Salt of the earth.


01:21:32.160 --> 01:21:36.836
I will marry the memsahib
to the first fakir I can find.


01:21:36.960 --> 01:21:40.555
The first thing I do
when we step off the plane.


01:21:46.760 --> 01:21:48.716
<i>(laughs)</i>


01:21:48.840 --> 01:21:51.274
What is so funny. Memsahib?


01:21:51.400 --> 01:21:54.153
- You are.
- Shahana!


01:21:54.280 --> 01:21:57.078
You are. With your stupid phrases.


01:21:57.200 --> 01:22:01.716
You're always encouraging us to fit in.
It worked. We do fit in.


01:22:01.840 --> 01:22:04.991
You're the one
who's stuck somewhere. Abba.


01:22:05.120 --> 01:22:07.429
Tell him.


01:22:14.200 --> 01:22:16.668
Tell him you don't want to go.


01:22:17.560 --> 01:22:22.475
What? He takes away my son
and curses me with daughters?


01:22:22.600 --> 01:22:28.277
- Be careful what you say, memsahib.
- We're not the ones lost. Abba. You are!


01:22:28.400 --> 01:22:32.313
She's been married to you
for nearly 20 years.


01:22:32.440 --> 01:22:37.468
And in all my life, Amma, I have
never heard you say what you want.


01:22:37.600 --> 01:22:39.750
Please. Amma. Tell him.


01:22:40.720 --> 01:22:44.474
Tell him, Amma.
Please. For once. Please. Tell him.


01:22:44.600 --> 01:22:47.194
Please. Amma.


01:22:47.320 --> 01:22:49.959
Tell him you don't want to go!


01:22:50.080 --> 01:22:52.719
Just tell him you don't want to go!


01:22:53.560 --> 01:22:55.471
Tell him!


01:22:55.600 --> 01:22:57.556
Please!


01:22:59.320 --> 01:23:01.515
Please. Amma.


01:23:03.280 --> 01:23:05.111
You're pathetic!


01:23:05.240 --> 01:23:08.789
Bangladesh is gone.
It's another time.


01:23:12.800 --> 01:23:15.598
<i>- (door slams)
- (Bibi) Amma.</i>


01:23:17.840 --> 01:23:19.910
She will be back.


01:23:28.080 --> 01:23:29.638
Shahana!


01:23:29.880 --> 01:23:31.632
Shahana!


01:23:46.840 --> 01:23:49.513
Shahana! Shahana!


01:24:00.840 --> 01:24:02.068
Shahana!


01:25:09.880 --> 01:25:11.836
Shahana!


01:25:22.240 --> 01:25:24.196
Shahana!


01:25:29.800 --> 01:25:32.553
Shahana. Stop.


01:25:46.080 --> 01:25:48.036
<i>(sobs)</i>


01:25:51.080 --> 01:25:53.150
I don't wanna go.


01:25:54.240 --> 01:25:56.196
Amma is here.


01:25:59.920 --> 01:26:01.876
Don't worrv.


01:26:10.520 --> 01:26:12.476
<i>(grunts)</i>


01:26:14.880 --> 01:26:17.713
Shahana is asleep now.


01:26:18.680 --> 01:26:21.035
She is bound to be nervous.


01:26:21.760 --> 01:26:23.910
She will settle later.


01:26:24.040 --> 01:26:27.510
- I know it is almost time...
- I know. I know how exciting it is.


01:26:27.640 --> 01:26:30.871
I have checked our passports
and tickets for the last time.


01:26:31.000 --> 01:26:33.468
- But I wanted...
- Let us look forward now.


01:26:33.600 --> 01:26:37.036
Just imagine a house in Dhaka,
holiday in Cox's Bazar.


01:26:37.160 --> 01:26:39.435
A little trip for the girls to Shundar Bon.


01:26:39.560 --> 01:26:42.279
They could see a real Bengal tiger.


01:26:42.720 --> 01:26:45.109
I should have said this before. I...


01:26:45.240 --> 01:26:48.073
You see. All these years...


01:26:49.440 --> 01:26:53.399
I dreamed of going home a big man.


01:26:53.520 --> 01:26:56.318
Only now.


01:26:56.440 --> 01:26:58.715
When it is finished for me...


01:27:00.960 --> 01:27:03.315
I realised what is important.


01:27:06.640 --> 01:27:10.076
As long as I have my family with me


01:27:10.200 --> 01:27:13.476
I'm strong as any man alive.


01:27:23.080 --> 01:27:26.356
What is all this "strong man" about?


01:27:26.480 --> 01:27:29.358
Do you think that is why I love you?


01:27:29.480 --> 01:27:31.152
You're coming home.


01:27:32.760 --> 01:27:34.591
This is my home.


01:27:38.640 --> 01:27:40.870
I cannot leave.


01:27:42.240 --> 01:27:44.310
I cannot stay.


01:27:49.760 --> 01:27:51.796
I cannot stay.


01:28:01.320 --> 01:28:03.550
Then you must take the plane.


01:28:12.760 --> 01:28:14.910
Allah has taken our son


01:28:15.040 --> 01:28:17.600
but he blessed us with daughters.


01:28:26.840 --> 01:28:29.638
We will always be here.


01:28:30.640 --> 01:28:32.596
<i>(sobs)</i>


01:28:43.680 --> 01:28:47.434
<i>(Nazneen) No one told me
there are different kinds of love.</i>


01:28:49.200 --> 01:28:51.953
<i>The kind that starts big</i>


01:28:52.080 --> 01:28:54.878
<i>and slowly wears away.</i>


01:28:55.000 --> 01:28:57.992
<i>That seems you'll never use it up</i>


01:28:58.120 --> 01:29:00.475
<i>and then one day it is finished.</i>


01:29:02.320 --> 01:29:07.997
<i>Then there is the kind
that you do not notice at first.</i>


01:29:08.120 --> 01:29:12.955
<i>But which adds a little bit
to itself every day.</i>


01:29:13.080 --> 01:29:15.514
<i>Like an oyster makes a pearl</i>


01:29:15.640 --> 01:29:17.949
<i>grain by grain.</i>


01:29:18.080 --> 01:29:20.116
<i>A lewel from the sand.</i>


01:29:21.080 --> 01:29:23.913
<i>That is the kind I have come to know.</i>


01:29:26.080 --> 01:29:30.039
<i>Sister. Thank you for your letter.</i>


01:29:30.160 --> 01:29:32.230
<i>For all your letters.</i>


01:29:50.320 --> 01:29:53.551
There has been a change of plan.


01:29:54.960 --> 01:29:57.315
I have suggested.


01:29:57.440 --> 01:30:00.432
And your mother has agreed.


01:30:00.560 --> 01:30:03.393
That the three of you come later.


01:30:07.200 --> 01:30:10.078
But who will cook for you. Abba?


01:30:10.200 --> 01:30:12.589
Who will cut your corns?


01:30:12.720 --> 01:30:16.679
Don't you know?
I'm a better cook than your mother.


01:30:19.760 --> 01:30:21.751
Be good girls.


01:30:21.880 --> 01:30:24.155
Do as your mother tells you.


01:30:24.280 --> 01:30:28.876
And do not think there is anything
you are not good enough for.


01:30:29.000 --> 01:30:31.389
Remember.


01:30:31.520 --> 01:30:33.476
Abba.


01:30:35.120 --> 01:30:39.830
<i>- (Bibi) How will we manage without you?
- Your mother is in charge.</i>


01:30:39.960 --> 01:30:42.030
I think you should be fine.


01:30:44.160 --> 01:30:47.675
Everyone thought I married
a simple girl from the village.


01:30:49.400 --> 01:30:51.356
But...


01:30:54.000 --> 01:30:56.070
That should do for now.


01:30:58.000 --> 01:31:00.798
- I'm sorry.
- Never be sorrv.


01:31:09.000 --> 01:31:10.672
<i>(Nazneen in Bengali)</i>


01:31:33.840 --> 01:31:37.071
<i>(Nazneen) When I was born,
the midwife said:</i>


01:31:37.200 --> 01:31:41.990
<i>"Dress her for her burial.
This scrap is too weak to feed. "</i>


01:31:42.120 --> 01:31:44.953
<i>"Take her to the hospital if you must."</i>


01:31:45.080 --> 01:31:47.514
<i>"No." said my Amma.</i>


01:31:47.640 --> 01:31:51.155
<i>"My child must not fight against her fate."</i>


01:31:51.280 --> 01:31:54.431
<i>"That way. She will be stronger."</i>


01:31:55.640 --> 01:31:57.995
<i>(Bibi) Shahana. Amma. Iook.</i>


01:31:58.120 --> 01:31:59.872
<i>And so I lived.</i>


01:32:04.160 --> 01:32:06.196
<i>Sister.</i>


01:32:06.320 --> 01:32:08.595
<i>I have this dream</i>


01:32:08.720 --> 01:32:11.154
<i>that you are always running...</i>


01:32:13.000 --> 01:32:17.437
<i>and I am torn between two worlds,
leaving you behind.</i>


01:32:20.720 --> 01:32:23.075
<i>But then I wake</i>


01:32:23.200 --> 01:32:27.751
<i>and see that it is not you
but me who has been running.</i>


01:32:30.240 --> 01:32:32.470
<i>Searching for a place</i>


01:32:32.600 --> 01:32:35.239
<i>that has already been found.</i>


01:32:41.480 --> 01:32:44.278
- I'm gonna get you!
- Shahana. No!


01:32:44.400 --> 01:32:47.233
<i># Dhol dhol dholoni</i>


01:32:48.800 --> 01:32:51.633
<i># Ranga mathay chironee</i>


01:32:53.120 --> 01:32:55.953
<i># Bor ashbay ekhonee</i>


01:32:57.440 --> 01:33:00.273
<i># Niye labay thokhonee</i>


01:33:01.680 --> 01:33:04.911
<i># Dhol dhol dholoni</i>


01:33:06.000 --> 01:33:09.197
<i># Ranga mathay chironee</i>


01:33:10.320 --> 01:33:13.153
<i># Bor ashbay ekhonee</i>


01:33:14.760 --> 01:33:17.274
<i># Niye labay thokhonee</i>


01:37:21.320 --> 01:37:24.278
Visiontext Subtitles: Margaret Burke

